  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Demonstrating C3 Living Units in Maputu and Beira</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Mozambique, there is an estimated housing shortage of 2 million and approximately 13.5 million people are living in unsuitable living conditions. The recent cyclone that hit the country ruined over 240,000 houses and the total damages for housing is estimated to be over 678 million US dollar. Under the brand of C3Living, Rendiz B.V. develops affordable flexible, transportable and sustainable living units using the cradle2cradle principle. The housing units may provide a solution to the affordable housing issues in Mozambique, including for low income households seeking to rebuild after the cyclone. Technical Assistance (DGGF-TA) provided support to develop demonstration units that meets local requirements. 4 houses were built and supported 14 people for the duration of the project, who also received training on how to do construction.</narrative>
  </description>
